le which the  defendants freely and publicly admit  they're conjuring movie was based on  does not at all jive with the real  historical facts this is a pattern of  deceit that is part of a scheme that the  wardens have perpetuated for years there  are no historical facts of a witch ever  existing at the perón farmhouse a witch  hanging herself possession satanic  worship or child sacrifice the New  England skeptical society launched an  investigation into the warns they looked  over all the evidence and case files  concluding that the Warrens were quote  at best tellers of meaningless ghost  stories and at worst dangerous frauds  brittle thinking he had a strong case  did what anyone would do sue Warner  Brothers for nine hundred million  dollars the case seemed like a slam dunk  it was clear Warner Brothers was using  the Warne stories image flaunting it  even in the posters and fairing Lorraine  Warren and director James Wan to various  press junkets been a big fan of  Lorraine's for a while  now if read stories and seen you know  movies that were based on cases that  Lorraine investigated in an interview  explaining how she prepare for the role  of Lorraine Warren actress Vera Farmiga  said quote primarily my research relied  on the non-fiction book the demonologist  I felt a sense of terror every time I  cracked it open I never read the book in  the sanctity of my home in April of 2017  Warner Brothers attempted to dismiss the  lawsuit in court but failed as US  District Court Judge John Gibney jr.  said in his ruling the court declines  the party's invitation to wade into the  truth or falsity of the Warne's  paranormal escapades or to parse the  resulting similarities between the works  at this stage of the case this type of  analysis which bears on evidence  presented and factual determinations is  better suited for summary judgment or  trial so this case was going to trial  and if Warner Brothers was to win they  would have to prove with evidence and  factual determinations that indeed this  exists alas the studio that brought us  Battlefield Earth and this  what's not up to the challenge in a  somewhat anticlimactic finish in  December of 2017 brittle and Warner  Brothers settled for an undisclosed  amount but the story gets more bizarre  turns out brittle wasn't behind the case  it was a disgruntled producer by the  name of Tony De Rosa Grund in 2014 de  rosa grande a producer on the conjuring  began a string of lawsuits against  Warner claiming money owed and hurling  accusations such as money laundering and  overt racketeering acts when those suits  were dismissed  DeRosa grunt tracked down brittle and  ultimately bankrolled the whole thing in  court documents to Rosa Grund allegedly  threatened to fire brittles attorney if  they sent information he had not  approved and instructed brittle to  withhold information and documents from  their own attorneys when the attorneys  reminded to Rosic run that brittle was  their client not to rosa grande he  texted good then get Gerald to [ __ ]  pay you oh yeah he doesn't have a pot to  piss in these new revelations combined  with the drop lawsuit spurred the judge  to order a forensic examiner to comb  over all the documentation and look for  altered or deleted documents so like an  old episode of scooby-doo there's no  real ghost in this story just a man  hiding behind a mask attempting to get a  good scare and a couple million dollars  thanks for watching I was really hoping  they would prove ghosts exist because  that would be cool I know this video is  a bit different than my normal ones but  tell me what you think in the comments  do you want more videos like this and  don't forget to Like and subscribe
 

